    "shadow": "Ambition read as pure acquisition costs you the people who would have carried you furthest, and they withdraw without ever explaining. What powers the climb is a hope that arriving somewhere will finally settle the question, so each achieved level is discounted within a fortnight and the reputation becomes one of restlessness rather than drive. Those who helped you notice they stopped hearing from you once the rung was reached, and the story travels. There is a private cost too: you experience your own life as a corridor, and people close to you feel like fixtures in a stage you are passing through. Being known as hungry works until someone needs to trust you with theirs.",
    "invitation": "Who helped you up and has not heard from you since? Send that person a real message before you chase down the next thing on your list. You are allowed to rise in a way that lifts the people underneath you. When your aspiration includes them, what kind of ascent becomes possible?"
