    "shadow": "Moods that arrive unannounced get read as instability, and colleagues start planning around your weather instead of your work. There is a story underneath in which things happen to you, so the difficulty gets narrated as fate and people slowly hear a complaint where they wanted a person. Those who tried to help and were rebuffed on a dark day rarely offer twice. The reputational cost compounds quietly: invitations thin, and nobody tells you it was the unpredictability rather than the ability. Being known as someone at the mercy of their own state is precisely the reverse of the freedom you are actually built for.",
